---
title: Admission & Pass Policy
description: Admission Policies and rules.
---

h1 Admission & Pass Policy General Policy

p An admission fee is charged to everyone upon entering Field Days grounds
  | every day from 7:00 a.m. until midnight.
  | EXCEPTIONS
  ol
    li Children age 5 and under will be always admitted FREE when accompanied by an adult.
    li Active 4-H members and leaders who are exhibiting and volunteering
      | every day will be admitted to the grounds free upon presentation of a special
      | colored 4-H/Fair Bracelet. One leader from each club will send a list of active
      | participating members and leaders by July 19th to: 4-H Fair Passes, UVM
      | Extension, 23 Pond Lane Suite 300, Middlebury, VT 05753. 4-H members
      | will receive their passes from their leader or department superintendent.
    li See specific policies (below).
      br
  | NOTE: Special individual rate of $10.00 applies to busloads or
  | groups of 20 or more people who have made prior arrangements.
p The payment of a one-day admission permits the individual re-entry on the
  | grounds during that same day and evening with hand stamp applied by Gate Admission personnel.
h3 Complimentary Passes
p.
  Any individual who claims that he/she should have a free Field Days pass
  will pay the regular gate admission charges, but should be advised to contact
  his/her department superintendent or the Field Days office. A special slip
  signed at the gate is used. A full refund of gate payments will be made and a
  Field Days pass issued if such an individual is so qualified.
h3 SPECIFIC POLICIES 
h4 Admit without Passes:
ol 
  li.
    Employed entertainment groups to which Field Days has been unable
    to send passes. Field Days will advise gate personnel (ticket sellers) of these
    specific groups.
  li Governor, driver, and assistants.
  li State Police.
  li Congressional delegations.
  li State Inspectors
  li Children 5 years of age and younger.
h4 Exhibitor Policies
ol 
  li.
    Free Exhibit Space — will be provided for UVM, the Vermont Dept. of
    Agriculture, and possibly others at the discretion of the board of directors.
    One (1) free season pass provided for each free exhibit space.
  li.
    Commercial Exhibitors — will receive two (2) free season passes and two
    (2) parking passes for each space purchased. Additional day passes may be
    purchased for $10.00 each.
  li
    | Adult Exhibitors — who participate every day. Includes: Open Dairy;
    | Open Beef; Sheep Show.
    ol
      li Those with the above exhibits may purchase a five-day pass for $25.00
        | each as follows:
        ul
          li 1 - 5 animals on exhibit: limit 2 passes
          li 6 - 10 animals on exhibit: limit 3 passes
          li 11 or more animals: limit 4 passes
  li All other youth and adult exhibitors — one (1) season pass per exhibitor.
  li.
    Non 4-H Youth Exhibitors — who pay no entry fee and who participate
    one (1) day only will receive one (1) free day pass through their Field Days
    Department Superintendent.
  li.
    Adult Exhibitors — who pay no show entry fees and who participate
    one (1) day only will pay the regular gate admission with no refund, with
    exception of hand mowing.
  li.
    Youth & Adult Exhibitors — who bring in and set up exhibits and remove
    them at the conclusion of Field Days are expected to do their set-up on
    Monday and tear-down after Field Days closes. Those who must enter on
    Saturday evening before the ticket booths close to claim their exhibits will
    be issued one (1) one day pass which may be used only for exhibit pickup
    admission. Examples: Crops, Flower Show, Vegetable Exhibits, Handcrafts,
    Foods, any static exhibits.
  li
    | Youth & Adult Horse Show Participants — entry fees are paid by these
    | exhibitors. Passes will be issued by the Superintendent of Horse Shows
    | according to announced rules, which have been approved by the Field Days
    | Directors, with the following exceptions:
    ol
      li Registered Horse Show advance entries (non 4-H’ers) will get one (1)
        | free day pass per rider.
      li.
        4-H Youth Horse Show riders may get, through their Horse
        Superintendent and with membership card shown, one (1) free day pass,
        and may purchase one (1) season pass for $25.00 at the discretion of
        the Horse Show’s Superintendent, season passes may be given to those
        entrants who have horses on the grounds for the entire Field Days.
  li.
    Maple Producers — if half (1/2) of the maple space is devoted to
    educational material, free season passes will be issued for that area. The
    remaining portion of the area will be treated as a concession. If less than half
    of the maple space is devoted to educational material, the entire building
    will be treated as a concession.
  li.
    4-H passes — see 4-H Rules Page
h4 Other Than Exhibitors
p.
  Those invited for demonstrations: (fashion show, parade, VIP’s, Dairy
  Queen, Miss Vermont, etc.); educational, religious - will be issued necessary
  free day passes by the department Superintendent or the person(s)
  responsible for the specific event. In the event gate admission has been paid,
  Field Days will make a refund upon verification, via the special form issued at
  the gate where admission was paid, of payment of said admission.
p.
  Holders of State Fair Assoc. passes admitted without charge at any time.
  Employed Entertainment Groups - see #1 under SPECIFIC POLICIES, or
  follow instructions of Field Days office.
p.
  Special season passes may be issued, at the discretion of the Board of
  Directors, to Field Days grounds neighbors at the rate of one (1) per family
  member living at home.
h2 Camping Fees
p The fees for camping on the grounds are $175 a week or $50 a night.
p Electricity, water, and gray/septic water pumped included. You must fill out
  | and send a form before July 22nd.
p.
  Camping spaces DO NOT include admission. You must buy a
  season pass for every person staying in the camper/tent.
